CORE
main.c
--unwind 4 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
A store at a symbolic index was recorded as a read of every element.

`slot[i] = 1` on a field-sensitive array becomes, for every element k,

    slot[[k]] == (i == k ? 1 : slot[[k]])

and materialising that right-hand side renames every element, emitting a
shared read for each. Those reads are the lowering carrying the untouched
elements forward; the program performs none of them. For reachability that
costs nothing -- only the value is consumed -- but the event set *is* the
property for data-race detection, so two threads storing to different
elements were paired on all of them.

Measured on this program before the fix: the single store produced 8
SHARED_READ(slot[[0..3]]) with no index guard against 12 SHARED_WRITE
carrying `curr % 4 == k`. The writes were already conditioned by
field_assignments_rec; the reads were not, and the asymmetry was the bug.

The base operand of a `with` at a non-constant index is now expanded with
`record_events` suppressed, so the values are produced and no events are
recorded.

Five earlier attempts at this family all gated reads on branch conditions and
all lost real races -- the goblint suite pairs `_nr` with `_rc` deliberately,
and a tool that gets one right by being imprecise gets the other wrong. This
one removes an event that corresponds to nothing instead of conditioning one
that does, and the discriminating pair confirms it: a variant where the
indices really collide (`% 1`) and one where both threads read the same index
both stay FAILED, as does goblint-regression/06-symbeq_10-equ_rc, the real
race that killed attempts 2 and 3.

libvsync/bounded_mpmc_check_full is the benchmark this cost: a correct queue
whose producers claim distinct slots with a CAS, reported as racing on them.
